From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Map edges drawn on straight, not mirrored (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mirrored past an edge, a map showed its own houses, ponds, paths, cliffs
and windmills again backwards (rejected on 2026-11-07; each place below
had its picture approved before this was made). Past an edge now the
map's strip by it goes on straight (Port_RenderExtrudedPart): each
polygon that reaches the border again and again, moved on by its own
width (a cliff's face, the ground by it, a row of trees drawn as one long
quad); what starts in the map's last column every tile; the trees in the
last two columns (or rows) whole, every 2 tiles (a tree is 4 quads of
1 3/8 to 2 1/2 tiles over one place; past the top or bottom a row of
them drawn as long leaning quads counts too); into a corner what goes on
both ways. A slope or wall along the border in its last column (facing
the border, not across it) isn't drawn on, its faces side by side made
teeth: the flat polygon at its top beside it along the border is drawn
again over its length instead (Port_MakeExtrudeFills).

Where: Route 204's two maps past their forest scenery; Floaroma Meadow
and Eterna Forest past every edge and corner (the forest was black past
its top and bottom); Hearthome's west, the mountain scenery beside its
north half (a purple plain) replaced by its west forest; the Cycling
Road and Valley Windworks past their scenery (the river goes on, and the
mountains south of Valley Windworks with it, Port_BelowExtruded); and
Amity Square. There the top-right map ends at the right in the plateau's
last cliff, sloping down to the border: past it, the bottom-right map's
upper terrace of trees goes on north instead (sPortExtrudeForests; that
map's model read whole if it isn't loaded), the cliff going down into it.
Nothing is mirrored now (sPortMirroredEdgeMatrices has no matrix; the
code is kept).

Each part is one copy of the map's model whose lists hold each polygon
again at every place it's drawn at, an MTX_TRANS between, drawn once (on
the PC 43 draws a scene to 2 at Amity Square's west edge). Copies are
made two shapes a scene ahead for the loaded maps by an edge, in either
half of them (Port_ExtrudeAhead), so they're made before the edge comes
into the view; one needed before that (after a warp) is made at once.
Each shape's list is read once for its cuts (NitroPort_Gx3dSurveyList;
on the PC 2.1 to 0.6 ms a copy).

On the PC the same pictures as the approved ones at every place, and the
same as before at Veilstone, Route 215, Solaceon, Jubilife, Floaroma,
Eterna, Route 210 and Hearthome's east side.
